    <string name="notification_app_translocated">Keryx is running from a temporary location. If Dropbox integration and similar features fail, move Keryx to the Applications folder and relaunch it.</string>
    <string name="notification_app_translocated_detail">macOS uses a mechanism called App Translocation to run apps launched directly from a disk image (DMG) or the Downloads folder from a random temporary location each time.\n\nBecause this changes Keryx’s actual path, the OS can’t deliver keryx:// links to it, which can prevent Dropbox or OneDrive integration (OAuth authentication) from completing.\n\nFix: copy Keryx.app to the Applications folder and launch it from there.</string>

